# EXAMPLE / TEMPLATE — copy or generate the real chain to `static/cert.pem`
# (the real cert.pem is git-ignored so you never commit deployment-specific files).
#
# Replace with the full X.509 certificate chain in PEM format.
#
# The file must contain the leaf certificate followed by any intermediate
# certificates, in order, ending at (but not including) the root CA.
#
# Example structure:
#   -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
#   <leaf certificate - your organisation's seal/EV cert>
#   -----END CERTIFICATE-----
#   -----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----
#   <intermediate CA certificate>
#   -----END CERTIFICATE-----
#
# To export from a PKCS#12 (.p12 / .pfx) file:
#   openssl pkcs12 -in your-cert.p12 -nokeys -chain -out static/cert.pem
#
# The leaf certificate's trust chain MUST anchor to a CA listed in the
# Gaia-X Registry (https://registry.gaia-x.eu/) — verify this before you buy.
